window.GDATA = window.GDATA || {};
window.GDATA[9] = {"units":{"1":{"title":"My Language - My Identity!","tests":[{"id":"1.1","title":"Vocabulary","words":[["a sense of belonging","aidiyyət hissi","чувство принадлежности","phrase","When I'm with my classmates, I feel a sense of belonging.","a feeling of being accepted and respected as a member of a particular social group, community, or place","ʌ sɛns ʌv bɪˈlɔŋɪŋ"],["confidence","özünəinam","уверенность","noun","After I practised riding my bike every day, I gained confidence.","the feeling of believing in yourself and your abilities","ˈkɑnfədɛns"],["connect","bağlamaq, əlaqələndirmək","связывать","verb","Your mother tongue helps you connect deeply with your culture and community.","to join or link together, or to feel close to someone or something","kəˈnɛkt"],["connected","bağlı","связанный","adjective","At the family picnic, everyone felt connected because of the warm family atmosphere.","related to or being part of a relationship with someone else","kəˈnɛktɪd"],["essential","vacib, zəruri","необходимый","adjective","Eating fruits and vegetables is essential for staying healthy.","very important and necessary","ɛˈsɛnʃəl"],["fluent","səlis","беглый (о речи)","adjective","Sally is fluent in Spanish.","able to speak or write easily and accurately","fluənt"],["hug","qucaqlama","объятие","noun","Speaking my mother tongue is like a warm hug from my home country.","an act of putting your arms around someone as a way of showing love or friendship","hʌg"],["proudly","qürurla","гордо","adverb","I proudly speak my mother tongue with my Azerbaijani friends.","in a way that shows pride","ˈpraʊdli"],["recognise","tanımaq","узнавать","verb","I could recognise my friend even with her new glasses.","to know somebody or something because you have seen or heard him/her before","ˈrɛkəɡˌnaɪz"],["relationship","münasibət","отношения","noun","My dog and I have a special relationship.","the way in which two or more people or things are connected","riˈleɪʃənˌʃɪp"],["relative","qohum","родственник","noun","My grandmother is my favourite relative.","a family member, such as a parent, brother, sister, aunt or uncle","ˈrɛlətɪv"],["roots","kök, mənşə","корни","noun","Understanding your cultural roots means knowing about the history of your family.","origin","ruts"],["treasure","xəzinə, dəyərli şey","сокровище","noun","It's like having a special treasure that I can share with others.","an important object that is collected or kept because it is beautiful or has personal meaning","ˈtrɛʒər"]]},{"id":"1.2","title":"Reading","words":[["alive","canlı, diri","живой","adjective","Your mother tongue keeps your cultural traditions alive.","having life; living, not dead","əˈlaɪv"],["certainly","şübhəsiz, əlbəttə","безусловно","adverb","Reading will certainly improve your vocabulary.","used to emphasise that something is definitely true or will definitely happen","ˈsɜrtənli"],["connection","əlaqə","связь","noun","Sarah felt a strong connection with her new friend at school.","the way in which two or more things are related","kəˈnɛkʃən"],["deeply","dərindən, çox","глубоко","adverb","When we are bored or tired, we don't breathe as deeply as we usually do.","very; very much","ˈdipli"],["fault","nöqsan, qüsur","недостаток, вина","noun","Not to know a mother tongue is a great fault before the nation.","a mistake or weakness","fɔlt"],["float","üzmək (suyun səthində), süzülmək","плавать (на поверхности), парить","verb","A water lily can float on the water.","to move slowly on water or in the air","floʊt"],["identity","kimlik","идентичность","noun","Each person has their own identity. I am proud to be me!","who or what somebody/something is","aɪˈdɛntəˌti"],["value","dəyər vermək","ценить","verb","Teachers value their students' hard work and effort.","to think that somebody/something is important","ˈvælju"],["water lily","su zanbağı","кувшинка","noun","When I was studying teaching, I heard about \"water lily children\".","a type of plant that grows in water, with large leaves and large, usually white flowers","ˈwɔtər ˈlɪli"]]},{"id":"1.3","title":"Grammar A","words":[["civilisation","sivilizasiya","цивилизация","noun","Every civilisation has its own language and culture.","a state of human society that is very developed","ˌsɪvəlaɪˈzeɪʃən"],["embarrassing","utandırıcı","неловкий, смущающий","adjective","Making mistakes in a new language is not embarrassing.","making you feel shy or uncomfortable","ɪmˈbɛrəsɪŋ"],["go hand in hand","bir-biri ilə sıx bağlı olmaq","идти рука об руку","phrase","The study says mistakes and learning a language go hand in hand.","to be closely connected with each other","goʊ hænd ɪn hænd"],["impressive","təsirli, heyranedici","впечатляющий","adjective","Speaking five languages is very impressive.","(of things or people) making you admire them, because they are very large, good, skilful, etc","ˌɪmˈprɛsɪv"],["opportunity","imkan","возможность","noun","Mistakes provide us with an opportunity to learn.","a time when a particular situation makes it possible to do or achieve something","ˌɑpərˈtunəti"],["perfect","mükəmməl","идеальный","adjective","You don't need to be perfect to speak a new language.","having everything that is necessary; complete and without faults or weaknesses","ˈpɜrˌfɪkt"],["provide","təmin etmək, vermək","предоставлять","verb","Mistakes provide us with an opportunity to learn.","to give something to someone or make it available to them for use","prəˈvaɪd"],["shelter","sığınacaq","приют, убежище","noun","The puppy found a home at the animal shelter.","a place to stay for people or animals without a home","ˈʃɛltər"]]},{"id":"1.4","title":"Grammar B","words":[["accent","aksent, tələffüz tərzi","акцент","noun","I don't have an accent when I speak English.","a way of pronouncing the words of a language that shows which country, area or social class a person comes from","ˈækˌsɛnt"],["accidentally","təsadüfən, bilmədən","случайно","adverb","I accidentally dropped my keys on the way home.","by chance or by mistake","ˌæksəˈdɛnəli"],["case","hal, vəziyyət","случай","noun","Experts say that might not be the case all the time.","a situation or example of something, especially something bad","keɪs"],["condition","vəziyyət, xəstəlik halı","состояние","noun","Reuben is not the only person to have this language condition.","the state that something or someone is in, especially their physical state","kənˈdɪʃən"],["enjoyable","xoş, zövqverici","приятный","adjective","Playing games with friends is always enjoyable.","giving pleasure","ˌɛnˈʤɔɪəbəl"],["fall into a coma","komaya düşmək","впасть в кому","phrase","Doctors were worried that he could fall into a coma.","to become unable to wake up, usually for a long time","fɔl ˈɪntu ʌ ˈkoʊmə"],["go into shock","şoka düşmək","впасть в шок","phrase","Some people go into shock after an accident.","to suddenly feel very surprised, upset, or unable to understand something","goʊ ˈɪntu ʃɑk"],["kick","təpikləmək, vurmaq (ayaqla)","пинать, ударить ногой","verb","A player from the other team didn't want to kick Reuben in the head.","to hit somebody/something with your foot","kɪk"],["memory","yaddaş","память","noun","Reading is a workout that improves memory.","your ability to remember things","ˈmɛməri"],["mysterious","sirli, anlaşılmaz","загадочный","adjective","Reuben woke up with a mysterious language condition.","difficult to understand or explain; strange or unknown","mɪˈstɪriəs"],["probably","ehtimal ki","вероятно","adverb","That's most probably your \"gut feeling\".","used to say that something is likely to happen or to be true","ˈprɑbəˌbli"],["trauma","travma, sarsıntı","травма","noun","Some people start talking in a different accent after a head trauma.","emotional shock and pain caused by an extremely upsetting experience","ˈtrɔmə"],["warmth","istilik, hərarət","тепло","noun","I felt the warmth of my family at the picnic.","a quality of being warm in temperature or feeling","wɔrmθ"]]},{"id":"1.5","title":"Listening","words":[["abstract","mücərrəd","абстрактный","adjective","Piraha doesn't have words for abstract ideas.","existing in thought or as an idea but not having a physical reality","ˈæbˌstrækt"],["completely","tamamilə","полностью","adverb","Their experience of the world is almost completely in the present.","in every way possible; in every part","kəmˈplitli"],["count","saymaq","считать","verb","They don't count how much food they have.","to say numbers one after the other in order","kaʊnt"],["jungle","cəngəllik","джунгли","noun","The jungle is full of tall trees and wild animals.","an area of tropical forest where trees and plants grow very closely","ˈʤʌŋgəl"],["stupid","axmaq, ağılsız","глупый","adjective","The Piraha are not stupid, they just have a different way of experiencing the world.","having or showing a lack of ability to learn and understand things","ˈstupɪd"],["tool","alət","инструмент","noun","This method is a great tool for group collaboration.","a piece of equipment that you use with your hands to help you do something","tul"],["tribe","tayfa","племя","noun","The head of the tribe made important decisions.","a group of people, often of related families, who live together, sharing the same language, culture, and history","traɪb"],["unlike","fərqli olaraq","в отличие от","preposition","Unlike every other human language, Piraha doesn't have words for abstract ideas.","different from; not similar to something else","ənˈlaɪk"],["weapon","silah","оружие","noun","They can walk into the jungle without a weapon.","any object used in fighting or war, such as a gun, bomb, knife, etc","ˈwɛpən"]]},{"id":"1.6","title":"Writing 1","words":[["additional","əlavə","дополнительный","adjective","I would like to get additional information about the course.","extra","əˈdɪʃənəl"],["appreciate","qiymətləndirmək, minnətdar olmaq","ценить, быть признательным","verb","I would appreciate your help.","to understand the value or importance of something or someone","əˈpriʃiˌeɪt"],["concise","qısa və aydın, yığcam","краткий","adjective","Your email should be clear and concise.","giving only the information that is necessary and important, using few words","kənˈsaɪs"],["include","daxil etmək","включать","verb","Decide which one to include.","to have someone or something as part of a group or set","ˌɪnˈklud"],["inquire","soruşmaq, məlumat istəmək","запрашивать, узнавать","verb","I am writing to inquire about the language courses you offer.","to ask for information about something","ˌɪnkˈwaɪr"],["intensive","intensiv","интенсивный","adjective","Do you offer an intensive English course in summer?","involving a lot of work or activity done in a short time","ˌɪnˈtɛnsɪv"],["necessary","zəruri, lazımi","необходимый","adjective","Thank you for taking the time to provide me with the necessary information.","that is needed for a purpose or a reason","ˈnɛsəˌsɛri"],["offer","təklif etmək","предлагать","verb","I am writing to inquire about the language courses you offer at My Language School.","to say that you are willing to give something to somebody","ˈɔfər"]]},{"id":"1.7","title":"Writing 2","words":[["private","fərdi, şəxsi","частный","adjective","I would like to take private lessons.","belonging to or for the use of a particular person or group; not for public use","ˈpraɪvət"],["regarding","haqqında, ilə bağlı","относительно","preposition","I am writing regarding your language courses.","about somebody/something","rɪˈgɑrdɪŋ"],["request","xahiş etmək, tələb etmək","просить, запрашивать","verb","I would like to request more information about the course.","to ask for something or ask somebody to do something in a polite or formal way","rɪkˈwɛst"],["salutation","müraciət forması (məktubda)","приветствие (в письме)","noun","Start your email with a salutation like \"Dear Sir or Madam\".","the words that are used in a letter to address the person you are writing to, for example 'Dear Sir'","ˌsæljʊˈteɪʃən"],["specific","konkret, dəqiq","конкретный","adjective","We use \"the\" with a specific noun.","detailed and exact","spɪˈsɪfɪk"],["subject line","mövzu sətri (e-poçtda)","тема письма","noun","Write a short and clear subject line for your email.","the short heading that indicates the topic or purpose of an email or letter","ˈsʌbʤɪkt laɪn"],["unnecessary","lazımsız","ненужный","adjective","Don't include unnecessary information in your email.","not needed","ənˈnɛsəˌsɛri"]]},{"id":"1.8","title":"Time to Watch","words":[["enable","imkan vermək","давать возможность","verb","Learning languages can enable you to communicate with more people.","to make something possible","ɪˈneɪbəl"],["enjoyment","zövq, həzz","удовольствие","noun","Reading for enjoyment is a great way to learn new words.","the pleasure that comes from doing or experiencing something you like","ˌɛnˈʤɔɪmənt"],["feedback","rəy, əks-əlaqə","обратная связь","noun","Ask your teacher for feedback on your writing.","advice or information about how good or useful something or somebody's work is","ˈfidˌbæk"],["figure out","anlamaq","разобраться","phrasal verb","I couldn't figure out the answer.","to understand or solve something by thinking carefully about it; to find an answer to a problem","ˈfɪgjər aʊt"],["fluency","səlislik","беглость","noun","Practice is the key to fluency in a new language.","the ability to speak, write, or understand a language easily and well","ˈfluənsi"],["have something in common","ortaq cəhəti olmaq","иметь что-то общее","phrase","Polyglots have something in common: they are not afraid of mistakes.","to have the same interests, ideas, etc. as somebody else","hæv ˈsʌmθɪŋ ɪn ˈkɑmən"],["imitate","təqlid etmək","подражать","verb","Listen to native speakers and imitate their accent.","to copy someone's actions, speech, or behaviour, especially in order to entertain people or to practise","ˈɪməˌteɪt"],["in small chunks","kiçik hissələrlə","небольшими частями","phrase","Learn new words in small chunks.","in small pieces or parts","ɪn smɔl ʧʌŋks"],["memorise","əzbərləmək","запоминать","verb","It is easier to memorise new words in small chunks.","to learn something so that you can remember it exactly","ˈmɛməraɪz"],["patience","səbir","терпение","noun","Learning to ride a bike takes practice and patience.","the ability to stay calm, especially when waiting for a long time or when dealing with problems or difficult people","ˈpeɪʃəns"],["polyglot","poliqlot","полиглот","noun","A polyglot is a person who can speak many languages.","someone who knows and can use several languages","ˌpɑlɪˈglɑt"],["random","təsadüfi","случайный","adjective","Don't learn random words; learn words you need.","happening, done, or chosen by chance rather than according to a plan","ˈrændəm"],["revise","təkrarlamaq","повторять","verb","Revise new words every day.","to look again at something you have studied, in order to remember facts or practise a skill","rɪˈvaɪz"],["wonder","maraqlanmaq, düşünmək","интересоваться, задаваться вопросом","verb","I wonder how polyglots learn languages.","to think about something and try to decide what is true, what will happen, what you should do, etc","ˈwʌndər"]]}]},"2":{"title":"Lost in a Book","tests":[{"id":"2.1","title":"Vocabulary 1","words":[["accept","qəbul etmək","принимать","verb","Anyone over 18 can apply, but not everyone will be able to accept the offer.","to agree to take something that is offered; to say yes to something","əkˈsɛpt"],["adventure","macəra","приключение","noun","The book is about a great adventure in a magical world.","an exciting and possibly dangerous experience or journey","ədˈvɛnʧər"],["battle","döyüşmək, mübarizə aparmaq","сражаться","verb","In the book, Harry and his friends battle the dark wizard Voldemort.","to fight against someone or something in a war or competition","ˈbætəl"],["bravery","cəsarət, igidlik","храбрость","noun","The story teaches us about bravery and friendship.","the quality of being brave; the ability to face danger without showing fear","ˈbreɪvəri"],["concentrate","diqqəti cəmləmək","сосредоточиться","verb","During the test, it's important to concentrate on each question.","to focus all your attention on something","ˈkɑnsənˌtreɪt"],["creature","məxluq, canlı","существо","noun","In the story, they meet a dangerous creature in the forest.","a living thing, real or imaginary, that can move around, such as an animal","ˈkriʧər"],["discover","kəşf etmək","открывать","verb","Astronauts go on space missions to discover more about space.","to find something for the first time; to learn about something that was unknown","dɪˈskʌvər"],["fiction","bədii ədəbiyyat","художественная литература","adjective","Fiction books take us on amazing adventures with unreal stories.","a type of literature that describes imaginary people and events, not real ones","ˈfɪkʃən"],["improve","yaxşılaşdırmaq","улучшать","verb","I will work hard to improve my skills and become a better reader.","to make something better or to become better in quality","ˌɪmˈpruv"],["increase","artırmaq, artmaq","увеличивать(ся)","verb","Reading every day can increase your vocabulary.","to become greater in amount, number, value, etc,","ˌɪnˈkris"]]},{"id":"2.2","title":"Vocabulary 2","words":[["kindness","xeyirxahlıq","доброта","noun","Auggie teaches us important things about kindness and friendship.","the quality of being kind","ˈkaɪndnəs"],["maze","labirint","лабиринт","noun","A group of children find themselves in a mysterious maze.","a complex network of paths or passages where it is easy to get lost","meɪz"],["mystery","sirr, müəmma","тайна, загадка","noun","It's like my very own out-of-this-world mystery!","something that is difficult to understand or explain put yourself in somebody's shoes to imagine yourself","ˈmɪstəri"],["put yourself in somebody's shoes","özünü başqasının yerinə qoymaq","поставить себя на чьё-то место","idiom","Reading fiction helps you put yourself in somebody's shoes.","to imagine yourself in someone else's situation in order to understand their feelings","pʊt ˈjɔrsɛlf ɪn ˈsʌmˌbɑdiz ʃuz"],["require","tələb etmək","требовать","verb","Learning math well will require some extra practice.","to need something; to depend on somebody/ something","ˌrikˈwaɪər"],["set an example","nümunə olmaq","подавать пример","phrase","Parents should set an example for their children.","to behave in a way that others should copy or follow","sɛt ʌn ɪgˈzæmpəl"],["solve","həll etmək","решать","verb","When I was able to solve my problem, it helped me be very confident.","to find an answer to a problem","sɑlv"],["way out","çıxış yolu","выход","noun","The children must find a way out of the maze.","a way of escaping from a difficult situation","weɪ aʊt"],["wizard","sehrbaz","волшебник","noun","The stories are about a young wizard named Harry and his friends.","(in stories) a man with magic powers","ˈwɪzərd"]]},{"id":"2.3","title":"Reading 1","words":[["based on","əsaslanan, əsasında","основанный на","phrase","Bookworms usually don't judge books based on their genre.","If one thing is based on another, it uses it or is developed from it","beɪst ɔn"],["bedtime","yatmaq vaxtı","время сна","noun","This study aims to learn how bedtime reading affects sleep.","the time when somebody usually goes to bed","ˈbɛdˌtaɪm"],["borrow","borc almaq (kitab və s.)","брать на время","verb","You can borrow books from the school library.","to take and use something that belongs to somebody else, and return it to them at a later time","ˈbɑˌroʊ"],["concentration","diqqəti cəmləmə, konsentrasiya","концентрация","noun","In a world where gadgets are shortening our attention span, we need to practise concentration.","?n/ the ability to direct all your attention on one thing, without thinking of other things","ˌkɑnsənˈtreɪʃən"],["dive into","həvəslə başlamaq","окунуться в","phrase","I love to dive into a good book.","to start doing something suddenly","daɪv ˈɪntu"],["effectively","effektiv şəkildə","эффективно","adverb","The more you read, the better you can communicate effectively.","in a way that produces a successful result","ˈifɛktɪvli"],["empathy","empatiya","эмпатия","noun","Empathy means being able to understand and share the feelings of someone else.","the ability to understand another person's feelings, experience, etc","ˈɛmpəθi"],["entertainment","əyləncə","развлечение","noun","For bookworms, reading is the best entertainment.","activities, performances, or events that provide enjoyment or relaxation","ˌɛnərˈteɪnmənt"],["inspire","ilhamlandırmaq","вдохновлять","verb","Reading books about people who have overcome difficulties can inspire us to do the same.","to give somebody the confidence or enthusiasm to do something well","ˌɪnˈspaɪr"]]},{"id":"2.4","title":"Reading 2","words":[["introduce","təqdim etmək, tanış etmək","представлять, знакомить","verb","Let's introduce our new friend to everyone in the class.","to present somebody/something to someone","ˌɪntrəˈdus"],["in turn","öz növbəsində","в свою очередь","phrase","Reading makes you a more informed person, in turn improving your conversation skills.","as a result of something in a series of events","ɪn tɜrn"],["motivational","motivasiyaedici","мотивирующий","adjective","Our teacher shares motivational stories that teach us to work hard.","= making somebody want to do something, especially something that involves hard work","ˌmoʊtəˈveɪʃənəl"],["overcome","öhdəsindən gəlmək","преодолевать","verb","With more practice, I can overcome any challenges that come my way.","to succeed in controlling a problem","ˈoʊvərˌkəm"],["picture","təsəvvür etmək","представлять","verb","Can you picture the main character?","to imagine somebody/something","ˈpɪkʧər"],["power","güc, qüdrət","сила, власть","noun","Books have the power to improve your vocabulary by introducing you to new words.","the ability to control people or things","paʊər"],["related to","ilə əlaqəli","связанный с","phrase","Fun is not important for them if it is not related to books.","connected with something else","rɪˈleɪtɪd tɪ"],["workout","məşq","тренировка","noun","Reading is a workout for your brain.","a period of physical exercise that you do to keep fit","ˈwɜrˌkaʊt"]]},{"id":"2.5","title":"Grammar A","words":[["beauty","gözəllik","красота","noun","Khan discovers the beauty in everyone and everything around him.","the quality of being pleasing and attractive, especially to look at","ˈbjuti"],["candy","konfet, şirniyyat","конфета","noun","The children were happy to get candy.","sweet food made of sugar and/or chocolate","ˈkændi"],["courage","cəsarət","смелость","noun","The hero of the story showed great courage.","the ability to do something dangerous or to face pain without showing fear","kərɪʤ"],["fortune","tale, bəxt","удача, судьба","noun","In the land of Surprisia, Khan learns about luck and fortune.","chance or luck, especially in the way it affects people's lives","ˈfɔrʧən"],["grab","qapmaq, cəld götürmək","хватать","verb","Grab your favourite book and start reading.","to take something with your hand suddenly","græb"],["historical","tarixi","исторический","adjective","I also like reading historical books.","related to events, people or things from the past; having importance in history","hɪˈstɔrɪkəl"],["humorous","yumoristik, gülməli","юмористический","adjective","This is a humorous story that will make you laugh.","funny or making you laugh","ˈhjumərəs"],["intelligence","intellekt, zəka","интеллект","noun","Emotional intelligence is the ability to understand, use, and manage our emotions.","the ability to learn, understand and use knowledge and information effectively","ˌɪnˈtɛləʤəns"],["knowledge","bilik","знание","noun","Reading increases general knowledge.","the information, understanding and skills that you gain through education or experience","ˈnɑlɪʤ"],["luck","şans","удача","noun","Good luck with your test!","good things that happen to you by chance, not because of your abilities","lʌk"],["truth","həqiqət","правда","noun","Patience and truth help Khan discover the true meaning of friendship.","the quality or state of being based on a fact","truθ"],["valuable","qiymətli","ценный","adjective","Emily's grandmother gave her a valuable necklace.","helpful, useful or important","ˈvæljəbəl"]]},{"id":"2.6","title":"Grammar B","words":[["adaptation","ekranlaşdırma, uyğunlaşdırma","экранизация, адаптация","noun","Sometimes a film adaptation is as good as the book.","a film, book, play, etc. that has been made from another film, book, play, etc","ˌædəpˈteɪʃən"],["author","müəllif","автор","noun","The amazing story was written by the young author who grew up in a small town.","a person who writes books, stories or articles","ˈɔθər"],["biography","tərcümeyi-hal, bioqrafiya","биография","noun","Whether it's a novel or a biography, as long as they're reading, they're happy.","a story of a person's life written by somebody else","baɪˈɑgrəfi"],["bookshop","kitab mağazası","книжный магазин","noun","Bookworms always enjoy visiting a bookshop.","a shop that sells books","ˈbʊkˌʃɑp"],["bookworm","kitabsevər","книжный червь","noun","My sister is a real bookworm.","a person who likes reading very much","ˈbʊkˌwərm"],["catchy","yadda qalan, cəlbedici","запоминающийся","adjective","The book has a catchy title.",".i/ pleasant and easily remembered","ˈkæˌʧi"],["genre","janr","жанр","noun","Bookworms usually don't judge books based on their genre.","a particular type or style of literature, art, film or music that you can recognize because of its special features","ˈʒɑnrə"],["in case","ehtiyat üçün, ... olarsa","на случай","phrase","They will bring a book with them wherever they go just in case they have some free time.","if something happens, or in preparation for when something happens","ɪn keɪs"],["judge","mühakimə etmək, qiymət vermək","судить, оценивать","verb","Bookworms usually don't judge books based on their genre.","to form an opinion about somebody/something, based on the information you have","ʤʌʤ"],["pick","seçmək","выбирать","verb","Bookworms love to pick a new book at the library.","to choose somebody/something from a group of people or things","pɪk"],["pleasure","zövq, həzz","удовольствие","noun","I get pleasure from spending time with my family.","a state of feeling or being happy","ˈplɛʒər"],["take a nose out of","(kitabdan) başını qaldırmaq","оторваться от (книги)","idiom","A true bookworm can't take a nose out of a book.","to stop reading or studying something","teɪk ʌ noʊz aʊt ʌv"],["top","ən yaxşı, ən yüksək","лучший, высший","adjective","Discuss and agree on the top 5 things you want to take with you.","the highest in rank, importance or quality","tɔp"]]},{"id":"2.7","title":"Listening","words":[["affect","təsir etmək","влиять","verb","This study aims to learn how bedtime reading can affect sleep.","to produce a change in something or someone","əˈfɛkt"],["aim","məqsəd qoymaq, hədəfləmək","стремиться, ставить целью","verb","This study wants to aim at understanding how bedtime reading affects sleep.","to try or plan to achieve something","eɪm"],["challenge","çətinlik","вызов, трудность","noun","Solving math problems is a challenge, but you can do it!","an invitation to somebody that they should enter a competition, fight, etc","ˈʧælənʤ"],["deliver","çatdırmaq","доставлять","verb","Should we deliver the package to your office or house?","to bring something to someone or somewhere","dɪˈlɪvər"],["diary","gündəlik","дневник","noun","A man finds money while reading his grandma's diary.","a special book where you write about your day, your thoughts and what you did","ˈdaɪəri"],["librarian","kitabxanaçı","библиотекарь","noun","The school librarian will provide us with new books to read.","a person who works in a library and helps people find books to read","laɪˈbrɛˌriən"],["siren","sirena","сирена","noun","We heard the siren of a police car.","a loud sound that makes a warning, like the sound of a police car","ˈsaɪrən"],["take part in something","nədəsə iştirak etmək","принимать участие в чём-то","phrase","Our teachers always encourage us to take part in different competitions.","to participate in something","teɪk pɑrt ɪn ˈsʌmθɪŋ"],["track","izləmək","отслеживать","verb","The app can track how many hours you sleep.","to follow the movements of somebody/something, especially by using special electronic equipment","træk"],["uniform","forma, uniforma","униформа","noun","He wore his police uniform and went to the police station.","a set of clothes that has to be worn by members of the same organisation or group","ˈjunəˌfɔrm"]]},{"id":"2.8","title":"Writing","words":[["branch","budaq","ветка","noun","Tim got stuck on a branch of the tall tree!","a part of a tree that grows out from the main part and has leaves or flowers on it","brænʧ"],["descent","eniş, aşağı düşmə","спуск","noun","Tim started his descent from the tall tree.","the act of moving or coming down from a higher place to a lower one","dɪˈsɛnt"],["ground","yer, torpaq","земля","noun","Tim felt really happy and proud as he stood safely on the ground.","the solid surface of the earth that you walk on","graʊnd"],["imaginary","xəyali","воображаемый","adjective","Third-person narratives are real or imaginary stories about another person.","existing only in your mind or imagination","ˌɪˈmæʤəˌnɛri"],["narrative","hekayə, nəql","повествование","noun","Choose one of the pictures and write a third-person narrative.","a story or a description of a series of events","ˈnɛrətɪv"],["safely","təhlükəsiz şəkildə","безопасно","adverb","I'm happy you all came back safely.","in a way that does not cause harm","ˈseɪfli"],["trunk","ağac gövdəsi","ствол","noun","Tim held on to the trunk of the tree.","the main part of a tree that supports branches as","trʌŋk"]]},{"id":"2.9","title":"Time to Watch","words":[["beagle","bigl (it cinsi)","бигль","noun","Our dog is a beagle with short legs.","a type of small dog with short legs, used in hunting","ˈbigəl"],["come out","çapdan çıxmaq, nəşr olunmaq","выходить (о книге)","phrasal verb","When will the new edition of the book come out?","to be produced or published","kʌm aʊt"],["comparison","müqayisə","сравнение","noun","Martin likes the comparison of the first edition with the latest edition.","the process of comparing two or more people or things","kəmˈpɛrəsən"],["complete","tamamlamaq","завершать","verb","Martin wants to complete his collection.","to finish or do all the parts of something","kəmˈplit"],["edition","nəşr","издание","noun","One of Martin's favourite books is an edition from 1972.","a special version or copy of a book, magazine or other things","ɪˈdɪʃən"],["fabulous","əla, möhtəşəm","потрясающий","adjective","He has a fabulous collection of books.","very good, excellent","ˈfæbjələs"],["own","sahib olmaq","владеть","verb","I want to own a pet dog because they are cute and fun.","to have something","oʊn"],["plenty of","çoxlu","много","phrase","Martin has plenty of books in different languages.","a lot or more than enough of something","ˈplɛnti ʌv"],["possession","mülk, sahib olunan şey","собственность","noun","Martin's most prized possession is in a language that he doesn't know.","something that you have","pəˈzɛʃən"],["prized","çox dəyərli","ценный","adjective","Martin's most prized possession is in a language that he doesn't know.","very valuable to somebody","praɪzd"],["remote","uzaq","отдалённый","adjective","He found a book from a remote country.","far away in distance or time","rɪˈmoʊt"]]}]},"3":{"title":"Why Do We Do That?","tests":[{"id":"3.1","title":"Vocabulary 1","words":[["act on something","nəyəsə əsasən hərəkət etmək","действовать в соответствии с чем-то","phrasal verb","It is not always a good idea to act on your gut feeling.","to do something as a reaction to a particular thing such a feeling or some information","ækt ɔn ˈsʌmθɪŋ"],["calm down","sakitləşmək","успокоиться","phrasal verb","Take a deep breath and calm down.","to become less anxious, or excited; to relax","kɑm daʊn"],["confusion","çaşqınlıq","замешательство","noun","There was some confusion about the homework.","kan'fju:.3?n/ a state of being unclear or uncertain; lack of understanding or order","kənfˈjuʒən"],["decrease","azaltmaq, azalmaq","уменьшать(ся)","verb","She has to make an effort to decrease doomscrolling.","to become smaller in size, amount, intensity, or importance","ˈdiˌkris"],["embarrassed","utanmış, pərt olmuş","смущённый","adjective","Why do people feel shy or embarrassed?","feeling ashamed or shy","ɪmˈbɛrəst"],["function","funksiya, iş prinsipi","функция","noun","Sleep helps your brain function better.","the way in which something works","ˈfʌŋkʃən"],["guide","istiqamətləndirmək, yol göstərmək","направлять","verb","When intuition takes charge, people's feelings and instincts guide their decisions or actions.","to give someone advice or help to do or understand something","gaɪd"],["gut feeling","daxili hiss, ürəyə dammaq","интуиция, внутреннее чутьё","phrase","Listening to your gut feeling is often advisable.","a strong belief about someone or something that cannot be explained and doesn't have to be decided by logical thinking","gʌt ˈfilɪŋ"]]},{"id":"3.2","title":"Vocabulary 2","words":[["instinct","instinkt","инстинкт","noun","Our brains scan all the potential dangers because it is a part of biological survival instinct.","the way people or animals naturally react or behave, without having to think or learn about it","ˈɪnstɪŋkt"],["recall","xatırlamaq","вспоминать","verb","I can't recall his name.","to bring the memory of a past event into your mind, and often to give a description of what you remember","ˈriˌkɔl"],["reminder","xatırlatma","напоминание","noun","I put a reminder on my phone.","things that help you to remember; signals to remember","riˈmaɪndər"],["scam","fırıldaqçılıq","мошенничество","noun","Later you learn that it was a bank scam.","an illegal way of making money, usually by tricking people","skæm"],["stretch something","bütün imkanlarını işə salmaq","напрягать (силы, возможности)","phrase","Difficult tasks stretch your mind.","to make use of all somebody's skill, intelligence, etc","strɛʧ ˈsʌmθɪŋ"],["take charge","məsuliyyəti öz üzərinə götürmək","брать на себя ответственность","phrase","Our class leader likes to take charge.","to take responsibility for controlling something","teɪk ʧɑrʤ"],["the case","həqiqət, vəziyyət","дело обстоит так","phrase","That is not the case.","true","ðʌ keɪs"],["warn","xəbərdar etmək","предупреждать","verb","Your gut feeling can warn you about danger.","to inform someone in advance of danger, problems, or risks","wɔrn"]]},{"id":"3.3","title":"Reading","words":[["inability","bacarıqsızlıq","неспособность","noun","The inability to stop laughing can put you in bad situations.","lack of ability to do something","ˌɪnəˈbɪlɪti"],["ineffective","səmərəsiz","неэффективный","adjective","All the methods I have tried were ineffective.","not producing the desired or results; lacking effectiveness","ˌɪnɪˈfɛktɪv"],["laughter","gülüş","смех","noun","The room was filled with laughter and joy.","the act or sound of laughing","ˈlæftər"],["long-term","uzunmüddətli","долгосрочный","adjective","Reading has many long-term benefits.","continuing a long time into the future","lɔŋtɜrm"],["lung","ağciyər","лёгкое","noun","Another theory is that yawning stretches the lung.","one of the two organs in the chest used for breathing","lʌŋ"],["organiser","planlaşdırıcı, orqanayzer","органайзер","noun","I write all my plans in my organiser.","an object that arranges things in an orderly manner","ˈɔːrɡənaɪzər"],["short-term","qısamüddətli","краткосрочный","adjective","Short-term memory helps you remember things for a few seconds.","lasting a short time","ʃɔrttɜrm"],["take something in","udmaq, içinə çəkmək","вдыхать, поглощать","phrasal verb","When we yawn, we take in more air.","to absorb something into the body, for example by breathing or swallowing","teɪk ˈsʌmθɪŋ ɪn"],["unborn","doğulmamış","нерождённый","adjective","Everybody yawns - from unborn babies to the oldest great-grandparent.","not yet born","ˈʌnˈbɔrn"],["yawn","əsnəmək","зевать","verb","Why do people yawn?","to open the mouth wide and take a lot of air into the lungs and slowly send it out, usually when tired or bored","jɔn"]]},{"id":"3.4","title":"Grammar A + Grammar B","words":[["avoid","qaçmaq, yayınmaq","избегать","verb","Try to avoid sad news before bedtime.","to try not to do something, or to try to stay away from something","əˈvɔɪd"],["doomscrolling","pis xəbərləri dayanmadan oxumaq (doomscrolling)","думскроллинг","noun","While reading the articles, I learned that it is called doomscrolling.","the activity of spending a lot of time looking at your phone or computer and reading bad or negative news stories","ˈduːmskroʊlɪŋ"],["dose","doza","доза","noun","My grandparents get some dose of sad news every day.","an amount or experience of something, often something bad or unpleasant","doʊs"],["potential","potensial, mümkün","потенциальный","adjective","Our brains scan all the potential dangers.","possible when the necessary conditions exist","pəˈtɛnʃəl"],["recent","son, yaxın vaxtlarda olan","недавний","adjective","How much money did he make from his recent exhibition?","happening or starting a short time ago; belonging to a time close to the present","ˈrisənt"],["scan","diqqətlə nəzərdən keçirmək","сканировать, просматривать","verb","Our brains scan all the potential dangers.","to examine something carefully","skæn"],["violence","zorakılıq","насилие","noun","Parvin cannot watch videos if there is violence.","forceful actions in order to hurt someone or that is likely to cause damage","ˈvaɪələns"],["violent","zorakı, qəddar","жестокий","adjective","Those people were very violent.","used to describe a situation or event in which people are hurt or killed","ˈvaɪələnt"],["assistant","köməkçi","помощник","noun","Now, let my assistant take you to the cardiologist.","a person who helps someone else in their work, tasks, or duties; a helper","əˈsɪstənt"],["cardiologist","kardioloq","кардиолог","noun","Now, let my assistant take you to the cardiologist.","a doctor who specialises in treating diseases of the heart","ˌkɑrdiˈɑləʤɪst"],["snore","xoruldamaq","храпеть","verb","My grandfather can snore very loudly.","to breathe in a very noisy way while you are sleeping","snɔr"]]},{"id":"3.5","title":"Listening + Writing","words":[["itch","qaşınmaq","чесаться","verb","When your hand begins to itch, some people say you will get money.","to have or cause an uncomfortable feeling on the skin that makes you want to rub it with your nails","ɪʧ"],["realise","həyata keçirmək, reallaşdırmaq","осуществлять","verb","They will realise exciting projects.","to achieve something you were hoping for","ˈriəˌlaɪz"],["shorten","qısaltmaq","укорачивать","verb","You can shorten the sentence.","to become shorter or make something shorter","ˈʃɔrtən"],["spill","tökmək","пролить","verb","Don't spill the water!","to cause a liquid or substance to flow out of its container and onto a surface","spɪl"],["superstition","xurafat, mövhumat","суеверие","noun","A superstition is a belief that some events bring good or bad luck.","the belief that particular events bring good or bad luck; the belief that explains the causes for events in ways that are connected to magic, not to science","ˌsupərˈstɪʃən"],["superstitious","mövhumatçı","суеверный","adjective","My grandmother is very superstitious.","believing in superstitions","ˌsupərˈstɪʃəs"],["contribution","töhfə","вклад","noun","Learning helps you make a meaningful contribution to society.","something that you do to help produce or achieve something together with other people, or to help make something successful","ˌkɑntrəˈbjuʃən"],["investment","investisiya, sərmayə","инвестиция","noun","In today's changing world, learning is a smart investment.","the act of putting money, time, or resources into something to make profit or get an advantage","ˌɪnˈvɛstmənt"],["life-long","ömürlük, ömür boyu","пожизненный","adjective","Life-long learning means that you never stop learning.","lasting or continuing for the entire duration of a person's life","laɪflɔŋ"]]},{"id":"3.6","title":"Time to Watch 1","words":[["alert","ayıq","бдительный","adjective","Cortisol makes us alert.","quick to see and understand and act in a particular situation","əˈlɜrt"],["critical","həlledici, çox vacib","критический, решающий","adjective","Sleep is critical for your health.","of the greatest importance to the way things might happen","ˈkrɪtɪkəl"],["cycle","dövr","цикл","noun","Our body clock works in a cycle.","a regular period of time during which an activity, job, etc. is done","ˈsaɪkəl"],["groggy","halsız, key","вялый, разбитый","adjective","If we don't follow the signals of our body clock, we might feel groggy.","weak or unable to think clearly or walk correctly usually because of tiredness","ˈgrɑgi"],["growth","böyümə, inkişaf","рост","noun","Sleep is important for the growth of children.","the growth of a person, animal, or plant is its process of increasing in size","groʊθ"],["hazy","dumanlı, aydın olmayan","смутный","adjective","My memory of that day is hazy.","not remembering things clearly","ˈheɪzi"],["internal","daxili","внутренний","adjective","It is very important to listen to your internal clock.","inside the body","ˌɪnˈtɜrnəl"],["jet lag","saat qurşağı yorğunluğu","смена часовых поясов (джетлаг)","noun","It can take some time and you can get jet lag.","the feeling of tiredness and confusion that people experience after making a long journey by plane to a place where the time is different from the place they left","ʤɛt læg"]]},{"id":"3.7","title":"Time to Watch 2","words":[["release","ifraz etmək, buraxmaq","выделять","verb","At night, the body can release melatonin.","to allow a hormone to flow out","riˈlis"],["repair","bərpa etmək, təmir etmək","восстанавливать, чинить","verb","During sleep, our body can repair itself.","to get something that is damaged or broken back into good condition, or to make something that is not working correctly work again","rɪˈpɛr"],["reset","yenidən qurmaq, sıfırlamaq","перезапускать","verb","When we travel across time zones, our body clock tries to reset itself.","to change the details of something","ˈrisɛt"],["respiratory rate","tənəffüs tezliyi","частота дыхания","phrase","When we sleep, our respiratory rate goes down.","the number of breaths taken per minute, typically measured as an indicator of respiratory health or function","ˈrɛspərəˌtɔri reɪt"],["restore","bərpa etmək","восстанавливать","verb","Sleep helps to restore the body.","to return something to an earlier good condition","rɪˈstɔr"],["strengthen","gücləndirmək","укреплять","verb","Knowing your history and culture can strengthen your roots.","to make something stronger or more effective, or to become stronger or more effective","ˈstrɛŋθən"],["wind down","dincəlmək","расслабляться","phrasal verb","In the evening, it is time to wind down.","to start to relax gradually after a period of hard work or a worrying situation","wɪnd daʊn"]]}]},"4":{"title":"The Sky's the Limit","tests":[{"id":"4.1","title":"Vocabulary 1","words":[["backpack","bel çantası","рюкзак","noun","I always take water in my backpack.","a piece of equipment that is carried on the back","ˈbækˌpæk"],["challenging","çətin","сложный","adjective","Schoolwork may be challenging for most of us.","difficult in an interesting way that tests your ability","ˈʧælənʤɪŋ"],["concept","anlayış, konsept","концепция","noun","The concept of living on Mars is very exciting.","an idea or a thought about something","ˈkɑnsɛpt"],["control module","idarəetmə modulu","модуль управления","noun","The astronauts sat in the control module of the spacecraft.","a part of a machine or device that helps to manage or operate it","kənˈtroʊl ˈmɑʤul"],["cope with something","nə iləsə öhdəsindən gəlmək","справляться с чем-то","phrase","It is very hard for an astronaut to cope with the stress in space.","to manage a difficult situation or problem","koʊp wɪθ ˈsʌmθɪŋ"],["cost","qiymət, xərc","стоимость","noun","The cost of a trip to space is very high.","the amount of money you need to pay for something","kɔst"],["explore","tədqiq etmək","исследовать","verb","Astronauts explore space.","to go on an adventure to discover new things or places","ɪkˈsplɔr"],["face","üzləşmək","сталкиваться с","verb","Astronauts face many challenges.","If you face something difficult, you have to take action","feɪs"],["goal","məqsəd","цель","noun","It's a big goal, but Asgardia is working hard for it!","something that you want to achieve","goʊl"],["incredible","inanılmaz","невероятный","adjective","Imagine you're an astronaut and you're on an incredible journey.","very surprising, especially in a way that you like or admire","ˌɪnˈkrɛdəbəl"]]},{"id":"4.2","title":"Vocabulary 2","words":[["involve","əhatə etmək","включать","verb","The project will involve all the students.","to include or be a part of something","ˌɪnˈvɑlv"],["Jupiter","Yupiter","Юпитер","noun","Jupiter is the largest planet in the solar system.","the largest planet of the solar system, fifth in order of distance from the sun","ˈʤupɪtər"],["liquid","maye","жидкость","noun","Scientists are sure that there is liquid water on Mars.","a substance that flows freely and takes the shape of its container, like water or juice","ˈlɪkwɪd"],["Neptune","Neptun","Нептун","noun","Neptune is very far from the Sun.","a planet in the solar system that is 8th in order of distance from the sun","ˈnɛptun"],["orbit","orbitdə fırlanmaq","вращаться по орбите","verb","Astronauts orbit the Earth every 90 minutes.","to move in an orbit around a much larger object, especially a planet, star, etc","ˈɔrbət"],["push the limits","sərhədləri aşmaq","выходить за пределы","idiom","Astronauts push the limits every day.","to try to do your best and go beyond what you thought you could do","pʊʃ ðʌ ˈlɪmɪts"],["research","tədqiqat","исследование","noun","In the research lab, scientists conduct experiments and learn new things.","a careful study of a subject, especially in order to discover new facts or information about it","ˈrisərʧ"],["Saturn","Saturn","Сатурн","noun","Saturn is a large planet that has rings around it.","a large planet in the solar system that has rings around it and is 6th in order of distance from the sun","ˈsætərn"],["survive","sağ qalmaq","выживать","verb","Can people survive on Mars?","continue to live or exist","sərˈvaɪv"],["Uranus","Uran","Уран","noun","Uranus is a very cold planet.","the planet in the solar system that is 7th in order of distance from the sun","ˈjɜrənəs"]]},{"id":"4.3","title":"Reading 1","words":[["atmosphere","atmosfer","атмосфера","noun","Our planet has everything we need to survive, like a breathable atmosphere, food, and water.","the mixture of gases surrounding the Earth or another planet, creating air","ˈætməsˌfɪr"],["breathable","nəfəs almağa yararlı","пригодный для дыхания","adjective","Mars doesn't have a breathable atmosphere.","(of the air) fit or pleasant to breathe","ˈbriːðəbəl"],["crew","heyət, ekipaj","экипаж","noun","Imagine that you are in the same crew capsule.","a group of people who work together on a ship, aeroplane, or other shared task","kru"],["data","məlumat, verilənlər","данные","noun","It had data about 18,000 citizens, the flag and the constitution of Asgardia.","facts or information, often in the form of numbers or statistics","ˈdætə"],["equipment","avadanlıq","оборудование","noun","Astronauts need special equipment to live in space.","the set of tools needed for a particular activity or purpose","ɪkˈwɪpmənt"],["exploration","kəşfiyyat, tədqiqat","исследование","noun","Let's go on an exploration and find new things!","the act of traveling to new or unfamiliar places in order to learn about them","ˌɛksplərˈeɪʃən"],["geologist","geoloq","геолог","noun","They have learned a lot about Mars from a robot geologist.","a scientist who studies the Earth's physical structure, substances, and processes","ʤiˈɑləʤəst"],["humanity","bəşəriyyət","человечество","noun","Space exploration is important for humanity.","people in general","juˈmænɪti"],["isolation","təcrid","изоляция","noun","Living in isolation means being by yourself without many people around.","the state of being alone or lonely","ˌaɪsəˈleɪʃən"]]},{"id":"4.4","title":"Reading 2","words":[["loneliness","tənhalıq","одиночество","noun","Astronauts on Mars may feel isolation and loneliness.","a feeling of being unhappy because you have no friends or people to talk to","ˈloʊnlinəs"],["poisonous","zəhərli","ядовитый","adjective","The air on Mars is poisonous for people.","causing death or illness if taken into the body","ˈpɔɪzənəs"],["radiation","radiasiya","радиация","noun","The radiation on Mars is dangerous for people.","energy in the form of waves or particles","ˌreɪdiˈeɪʃən"],["settlement","yaşayış məntəqəsi","поселение","noun","Settlement is a place where people build homes and live.","a place to live","ˈsɛtəlmənt"],["simulate","simulyasiya etmək, təqlid etmək","моделировать, имитировать","verb","Over the past twenty years, we've had many missions to simulate life on Mars.","to create particular conditions that exist in real life usually for study or training purposes","ˈsɪmjəˌleɪt"],["simulation","simulyasiya","симуляция","noun","I love playing simulation games on the computer.","a situation in which a particular set of conditions is created artificially in order to study or experience something that could exist in reality","ˌsɪmjəˈleɪʃən"],["take place","baş vermək","происходить","phrase","The International Astronautical Congress will take place in Baku.","to happen","teɪk pleɪs"],["waste","israf","трата","noun","Some people think Mars exploration is a waste of money.","a bad use of something valuable","weɪst"]]},{"id":"4.5","title":"Grammar A","words":[["available","mövcud","доступный","adjective","Water is not available on Mars.","that you can get, buy or find","əˈveɪləbəl"],["daily","gündəlik","ежедневный","adjective","In the morning, astronauts are given their daily tasks by ground control.","happening, done or produced every day","ˈdeɪli"],["fan","ventilyator","вентилятор","noun","There is a fan in every room of the space station.","a machine that creates a current of air","fæn"],["flavour","dad","вкус","noun","Food in space has less flavour.","the taste of a particular food or drink","ˈfleɪvər"],["get used to something","nəyəsə öyrəşmək","привыкать к чему-то","phrasal verb","Astronauts need time to get used to microgravity.","to adapt to a new situation or experience","gɪt juzd tɪ ˈsʌmθɪŋ"],["interaction","qarşılıqlı əlaqə","взаимодействие","noun","The friendly interaction between the students made the school day fun.","the act of communicating with somebody","ˌɪnərˈækʃən"],["microgravity","mikroqravitasiya (çəkisizlik)","микрогравитация","noun","In microgravity, astronauts float in the space station.","very weak gravity (= the force that makes things fall to the ground)","ˌmaɪkroʊˈɡrævɪti"],["monitor","nəzarət etmək, izləmək","контролировать, наблюдать","verb","Mission control on Earth can monitor the space station.","to watch and check something carefully over a period of time","ˈmɑnətər"],["regular","adi, müntəzəm","обычный, регулярный","adjective","They get dressed before they eat breakfast, much like a regular day on Earth.","happening or doing something often","ˈrɛgjələr"],["store","saxlamaq","хранить","verb","Astronauts store food and water on the space station.","to put or keep things in a special place for use in the future","stɔr"],["supply","təchiz etmək","снабжать","verb","Before the trip, make sure you supply everyone with water.","to provide something that is needed","səˈplaɪ"]]},{"id":"4.6","title":"Grammar B","words":[["astronautical","astronavtika ilə bağlı","астронавтический","adjective","Baku hosted the International Astronautical Congress.","relating to the design, construction, or operation of spacecraft or space travel","ˌæstrəˈnɑtɪkəl"],["attend","iştirak etmək","посещать, присутствовать","verb","More than 3,200 guests came to attend the opening ceremony.","to be present at an event, gathering, or activity","əˈtɛnd"],["banner","pankart, baner","баннер","noun","There was a colourful banner on every street of Baku.","a long piece of cloth with words written on it","ˈbænər"],["casual","gündəlik, qeyri-rəsmi","повседневный","adjective","Students wore casual clothes on the trip.","not formal","ˈkæʒəwəl"],["educational","təhsilə aid, maarifləndirici","образовательный","adjective","Special space programs will help students participate in educational space projects.","connected with education","ˌɛʤəˈkeɪʃənəl"],["excitement","həyəcan","волнение","noun","The excitement grew as the class prepared for the art exhibition.","the state of feeling or showing happiness","ɪkˈsaɪtmənt"],["expert","mütəxəssis, ekspert","эксперт","noun","He was sent to space to operate the instruments because he was an expert.","a person who has a high level of skill, knowledge, or expertise in a particular subject or activity","ˈɛkspərt"],["global","qlobal, ümumdünya","глобальный","adjective","Space exploration is a global goal.","covering or affecting the whole world","ˈgloʊbəl"],["hold","keçirmək (tədbir)","проводить (мероприятие)","verb","Baku will hold the International Astronautical Congress.","to have a meeting, competition, conversation, etc","hoʊld"],["local","yerli","местный","adjective","The local police are searching for the criminals.","connected with the particular place or area that you are talking about or with the place where you live","ˈloʊkəl"],["operate","idarə etmək, işlətmək","управлять, работать с","verb","He was sent to space to operate the instruments.","to use or control a machine or make it work","ˈɔpərˌeɪt"],["prestigious","nüfuzlu, prestijli","престижный","adjective","The International Astronautical Congress is a prestigious event.","respected and admired as very important or of very high quality","pərˈstiʤəs"],["selection","seçim","отбор","noun","After a long selection process, he was chosen as an astronaut.","the act of choosing someone or something","səˈlɛkʃən"]]},{"id":"4.7","title":"Listening","words":[["announcement","elan","объявление","noun","Within 40 hours of the project's announcement in 2016, 100,000 people applied for citizenship.","something that someone says officially, giving information about something apply for citizenship to ask to become a citizen of a country","əˈnaʊnsmɛnt"],["billionaire","milyarder","миллиардер","noun","He is also a billionaire.","a person who has money, property, etc. that is worth at least 1,000,000,000 dollars, pounds, euros, etc","ˌbɪljəˈnɛr"],["constitution","konstitusiya","конституция","noun","According to the constitution, their mission is to create peace in space.","the system of laws and basic principles that a state, a country or an organisation is governed by","ˌkɑnstəˈtuʃən"],["equal","bərabər","равный","adjective","Their mission is to create peace in space and equal opportunities for Asgardians.","the same in size, quantity, value, etc. as something else","ˈikwəl"],["found","təsis etmək","основывать","verb","Who decided to found Asgardia?","to establish something for the first time","faʊnd"],["founder","təsisçi, banisi","основатель","noun","The founder of Asgardia is a scientist.","a person who starts an organisation, institution, etc","ˈfaʊndər"],["resident","sakin","житель","noun","The person who lives in the neighbourhood is called a resident.","a person who lives in a particular place, such as a city or a country","ˈrɛzɪdənt"],["satellite","peyk","спутник","noun","A small satellite called Asgardia-1 was sent into space.","an electronic device that is sent into space and moves around the Earth or another planet","ˈsætəˌlaɪt"]]},{"id":"4.8","title":"Writing","words":[["alien","yadplanetli","инопланетянин","noun","Imagine that you are a journalist and you are about to conduct an interview with an alien.","a creature from a different planet or world","ˈeɪliən"],["attractive","cəlbedici","привлекательный","adjective","Space travel is very attractive for young people.","having qualities that make something seem interesting","əˈtræktɪv"],["bend down","əyilmək","наклоняться","phrasal verb","I had to bend down to pick up my keys.","to lower your body or part of your body","bɛnd daʊn"],["closet","paltar şkafı","шкаф","noun","Late one night, I heard music coming from my closet.","a cupboard or wardrobe, especially one tall enough to walk into","ˈklɑzət"],["drop","düşürmək, yerə salmaq","ронять","verb","Don't drop them or it will bring bad luck.","to fall or allow something to fall by accident","drɔp"],["object","əşya, obyekt","объект, предмет","noun","After the object disappeared, I ran all the way home.","a thing that you can see or touch, but that is not alive","ˈɑbʤɛkt"],["out-of-this-world","əla, möhtəşəm","потрясающий","idiom","It's like my very own out-of-this-world mystery!","extremely good or impressive; fantastic","aʊtʌvðɪswɜrld"],["shiny","parlaq","блестящий","adjective","I saw a shiny, round object flying above my head.","bright because it reflects light","ˈʃaɪni"]]},{"id":"4.9","title":"Time to Watch","words":[["blow one's mind","heyrətə gətirmək","поражать","idiom","This video will blow your mind!","to greatly surprise or impress someone","bloʊ wʌnz maɪnd"],["booster","sürətləndirici raket","ракета-ускоритель","noun","The booster gives the rocket extra power.","a rocket that gives a spacecraft extra power when it leaves the Earth","ˈbustər"],["co-founder","həmtəsisçi","соучредитель","noun","He is the co-founder of a space company.","a person who helps to found an organisation or company along with others","koʊˈfaʊndər"],["descend","enmək","спускаться","verb","The spaceship began to descend.","to move or fall downwards","dɪˈsɛnd"],["insane","ağlasığmaz, dəlilik","безумный","adjective","This is insane!","crazy","ˌɪnˈseɪn"],["launch","buraxılış","запуск","noun","We watched the launch of the rocket.","an occasion when a spacecraft is sent into space","lɔnʧ"],["on board","göyərtədə","на борту","phrase","There are three astronauts on board.","on or ina ship, an aircraft or a train","ɔn bɔrd"],["spin","fırlanmaq","вращаться","verb","In space, the astronauts can spin and float in the air.","to turn or cause to turn around quickly","spɪn"],["stranger","yad adam, tanımadığı adam","незнакомец","noun","Next to me in the capsule was a stranger.","a person whom one does not know","ˈstreɪnʤər"],["unbelievable","inanılmaz","невероятный","adjective","Unbelievable! I can't believe it.","difficult to believe","ˌənbəˈlivəbəl"],["vibrate","titrəmək","вибрировать","verb","The rocket started to vibrate during the launch.","to move or make something move from side to side very quickly and with small movements","ˈvaɪbreɪt"]]}]},"5":{"title":"Worth a Thousand Words","tests":[{"id":"5.1","title":"Vocabulary","words":[["admire","heyran olmaq","восхищаться","verb","People admire his paintings.","to look at something and think that it is attractive","ædˈmaɪr"],["artwork","sənət əsəri","произведение искусства","noun","We all admired the artwork in the school hallway.","work of art, especially one in a museum","ˈɑrtˌwərk"],["bead","muncuq","бусина","noun","She made a picture with every colourful bead she had.","a small piece of glass, wood, etc., with a hole through it, that can be put on a string with others of the same type and worn as jewellery, etc","bid"],["consider","hesab etmək","считать","verb","Experts consider the old books valuable.","to think of somebody/ something in a particular way","kənˈsɪdər"],["crayon","rəngli karandaş","цветной карандаш","noun","Inside the gift was a crayon for every child.","a coloured pencil used for drawing","kreɪɑn"],["express","ifadə etmək","выражать","verb","Some children express themselves through drawing pictures.","to show a feeling, an opinion, etc. by words, looks or actions","ɪkˈsprɛs"],["fashion","moda","мода","noun","She wants to work in fashion and design clothes.","the business of making or selling clothes in new and different styles","ˈfæʃən"],["filled with","dolu","наполненный","phrase","The room was filled with laughter and joy during the birthday party.","full of something","fɪld wɪθ"],["imagination","təxəyyül","воображение","noun","Yusif used his imagination to turn a simple cardboard box into a box for his toys.","something that you have imagined rather than something that exists","ˌɪˌmæʤəˈneɪʃən"],["inspiring","ilhamverici","вдохновляющий","adjective","His story is very inspiring.","exciting and encouraging you to do or feel something","ˌɪnˈspaɪərɪŋ"],["mural","divar rəsmi","фреска, настенная роспись","noun","There is a big mural on the wall of our school.","a big and colourful painting on a wall that tells a story or shares a message","mˈjʊrəl"],["screw","vint","винт, шуруп","noun","He used a screw to join two pieces of wood.","a thin, pointed piece of metal with a raised edge twisting round along its length and a flat top with a cut in it, used to join things together, especially pieces of wood","skru"],["struggle","çətinlik çəkmək","бороться, с трудом справляться","noun","Some students struggle with their homework, but they never give up.","a hard fight in which people try to get or achieve something","ˈstrʌgəl"]]},{"id":"5.2","title":"Reading","words":[["bull","buğa","бык","noun","Picasso made a bull's head from a bicycle.","the male of any animal in the cow family","bʊl"],["can","qutu, konserv bankası","банка","noun","The artist made a sculpture from an old can.","a metal or plastic container","kæn"],["nail","mismar","гвоздь","noun","Picasso did amazing things like drawing with a nail.","a small thin pointed piece of metal with a flat head, used for joining pieces of wood together or hanging things on a wall","neɪl"],["polio","poliomielit (uşaq iflici)","полиомиелит","noun","When Kahlo was six years old, she had polio.","a disease that affects the central nervous system and can cause temporary or permanent paralysis (= loss of control or feeling in part or most of the body)","ˈpoʊliˌoʊ"],["professional","peşəkar","профессиональный","adjective","Geysar Kashiyeva is considered the first professional Azerbaijani woman artist.","showing that somebody is well trained and has a lot of skills","prəˈfɛʃənəl"],["repression","repressiya","репрессия","noun","During the repression in the 1930s, most of her paintings got lost.","the act of using force to control a group of people and limit their freedom","riˈprɛʃən"],["self-portrait","avtoportret","автопортрет","noun","Frida Kahlo painted a self-portrait.","a painting, etc. that you do of yourself","sɛlfˈpɔrtrət"],["wrapped","bükülmüş","завёрнутый","adjective","The gift was wrapped in a newspaper, giving it a unique touch.","covered with material","ræpt"]]},{"id":"5.3","title":"Grammar A","words":[["attic","çardaq","чердак","noun","We had no idea there was such a special painting in our attic.","the space or room at the top of a building, under the roof, often used for storing things","ˈætɪk"],["carefully","diqqətlə","внимательно, осторожно","adverb","The painting has been carefully examined by experts.","with great attention","ˈkɛrfəli"],["celebrity","məşhur adam","знаменитость","noun","I know I am a celebrity, but I also need some privacy.","someone who is famous, especially in the entertainment business","səˈlɛbrɪti"],["damage","zədələmək, ziyan vurmaq","повреждать","verb","Be careful not to damage the painting.","to harm or spoil something","ˈdæmɪʤ"],["dusty","tozlu","пыльный","adjective","The old painting in the attic was very dusty.","covered in dust","ˈdʌsti"],["owner","sahib","владелец","noun","Mrs Johnson, the old owner, had no idea about the special painting.","someone who owns something","ˈoʊnər"],["privacy","şəxsi həyat, təklik","личная жизнь, уединение","noun","I know I am a celebrity, but I also need some privacy.","the state of being free from the attention of the public","ˈpraɪvəsi"],["steal","oğurlamaq","красть","verb","Someone tried to steal a famous painting from the museum.","to take something without the permission or knowledge of the owner and keep it","stil"]]},{"id":"5.4","title":"Grammar B","words":[["adult","yetkin, böyük insan","взрослый","noun","Kids can be more emotionally intelligent than an adult.","a fully grown person","ˈædəlt"],["carve","oymaq, yonmaq","вырезать (из камня, дерева)","verb","The sculptor wanted to carve a statue from marble.","to make objects by cutting away material from a piece of wood or stone, or another hard material","kɑrv"],["display","nümayiş etdirmək, sərgiləmək","выставлять","verb","The museum will display the paintings next month.","to put something in a place where people can see it easily; to show something to people","dɪˈspleɪ"],["exhibit","eksponat","экспонат","noun","Don't touch any exhibit in the museum.","an object that is shown to the public in a museum, etc","ɪgˈzɪbɪt"],["extract","çıxarmaq, hasil etmək","добывать","verb","Workers extract marble from the ground.","to remove or obtain a substance from something, for example by using an industrial or a chemical process","ˈɛkˌstrækt"],["fire escape","yanğın pilləkəni","пожарная лестница","noun","The children were playing on the fire escape.","metal stairs or a ladder on the outside of a building that people can use to escape from a fire","faɪər ɪˈskeɪp"],["grown-up","böyük, yetkin adam","взрослый","noun","Ask a grown-up for help.","an adult","ˈɡroʊn ʌp"],["marble","mərmər","мрамор","noun","There's a beautiful marble fountain in the middle of the park.","a type of hard stone that is usually white and often has coloured lines in it","ˈmɑrbəl"],["melt","ərimək, əritmək","таять, плавить","verb","Chocolate can melt in the sun.","to become or make something become liquid as a result of heating","mɛlt"],["press","basmaq, sıxmaq","нажимать, давить","verb","Don't press the paint too hard on the canvas.","to push something with strength","prɛs"],["sculptor","heykəltəraş","скульптор","noun","The sculptor carved a statue from marble.","a person who makes sculptures","ˈskʌlptər"],["sharp","iti","острый","adjective","Be careful, the knife is very sharp.","having a thin point that can cut something or make a hole in something","ʃɑrp"],["statue","heykəl","статуя","noun","There is a famous statue in the middle of the square.","an object made from a hard material, especially stone or metal, to look like a person or animal","ˈstæˌʧu"],["workspace","iş yeri","рабочее место","noun","The workspace must be left tidy after completing the activity.","the office, desk, etc. where somebody works","ˈwɜːrkspeɪs"]]},{"id":"5.5","title":"Listening","words":[["effect","təsir, nəticə","эффект, влияние","noun","The good news is that the effect of Stendhal syndrome doesn't last long.","a change that somebody or something causes in somebody or something else; a result","ˈifɛkt"],["faint","huşunu itirmək","падать в обморок","verb","Some visitors faint when they see great works of art.","to become unconscious when not enough blood is going to your brain, usually because of the heat, a shock, etc","feɪnt"],["last","davam etmək, sürmək","длиться","verb","The effects of Stendhal syndrome don't last long.","to continue for a particular period of time","læst"],["pen name","təxəllüs, ləqəb","псевдоним","noun","Stendhal is the pen name of a French writer.","an invented name used by a writer when publishing something","pɛn neɪm"],["persistence","əzmkarlıq, israrlılıq","настойчивость","noun","Success needs patience and persistence.","the fact of continuing to try to do something despite difficulties, especially when other people are against you","pərˈsɪstəns"],["rare","nadir","редкий","adjective","This is a rare book.","not done, seen, happening, etc. very often","rɛr"],["sweat","tərləmək","потеть","verb","We sweat when we play outside on hot days.","to produce liquid on skin","swɛt"],["syndrome","sindrom","синдром","noun","This syndrome has other names such as Florence syndrome or museum disease.","a set of physical conditions that show you have a particular disease or medical problem","ˈsɪnˌdroʊm"]]},{"id":"5.6","title":"Writing","words":[["breathtaking","nəfəskəsən, heyranedici","захватывающий","adjective","The view of the city from the top was breathtaking.","extremely exciting, beautiful or surprising","ˈbrɛθˌteɪkɪŋ"],["energetic","enerjili","энергичный","adjective","The city is energetic and busy.","having or needing a lot of energy","ˌɛnərˈʤɛtɪk"],["honk","siqnal vermək (maşın)","сигналить","verb","Outside my house, I hear cars honk loudly.","If a car horn honks, it makes a short, loud sound","hɔŋk"],["messy","qarışıq, səliqəsiz","грязный, неряшливый","adjective","The science experiment got a little messy.","dirty and/or untidy","ˈmɛsi"],["peaceful","sakit, dinc","мирный, спокойный","adjective","In the painting, I can see green grass and colourful flowers in a peaceful space.","quiet and calm","ˈpisfəl"],["sidewalk","səki","тротуар","noun","I found some money on the sidewalk today.","a flat part at the side of a road for people to walk on","ˈsaɪdˌwɔk"],["spot","yer, məkan","место","noun","This park is my favourite spot in the city.","a particular area or place","spɑt"],["wooden","taxta","деревянный","adjective","There are comfortable wooden benches in the park.","made of wood","ˈwʊdən"]]},{"id":"5.7","title":"Time to Watch","words":[["canvas","kətan","холст","noun","She paints on a big canvas.","a strong material used by artists for painting on","ˈkænvəs"],["crawl","sürünmək","ползать","verb","Before children learn to walk, they crawl.","to move forward on your hands and knees or with your body close to the ground","krɔl"],["critic","tənqidçi","критик","noun","The art critic liked the young artist's paintings.","someone whose job is to give their opinion about something, especially films, books, music, etc","ˈkrɪtɪk"],["decade","onillik","десятилетие","noun","She has painted for a decade.","a period of ten years","ˈdɛkeɪd"],["dilemma","dilemma","дилемма","noun","I have a dilemma: should I study art or music?","a situation in which a difficult choice has to be made between two different things","dɪˈlɛmə"],["encourage","həvəsləndirmək","поощрять","verb","Her parents encourage her to paint.","to give confidence or motivation to someone to do something","ɪnˈkɜrəʤ"],["envy","paxıllıq, qısqanclıq","зависть","noun","Some artists looked at her success with envy.","feeling very jealous of someone else's success","ˈɛnvi"],["fetch","gedib gətirmək","сходить и принести","verb","Can you fetch my paints from the other room?","to go to another place to get somebody or something to bring them/it back","fɛʧ"],["fluffy","tüklü, yumşaq","пушистый","adjective","The cat in the painting looks soft and fluffy.","covered in very soft fur or feathers","ˈflʌfi"],["tutor","repetitor","репетитор","verb","My brother has a math tutor.","to teach a child outside of school","ˈtutər"],["universe","kainat","вселенная","noun","When she paints, she thinks about the Universe.","everything that exists, including all stars, planets, galaxies and space","ˈjunəˌvərs"],["question","sorğu-sual etmək, sual vermək","допрашивать, задавать вопросы","verb","The journalist wanted to question the young artist about her paintings.","to ask somebody questions about something, especially officially","kˈwɛʃən"],["violin","skripka","скрипка","noun","She plays the violin beautifully.","a musical instrument with strings, which you hold under your chin and play with a bow","vaɪəˈlɪn"]]}]},"6":{"title":"Shine with the Right Skills","tests":[{"id":"6.1","title":"Vocabulary 1","words":[["acquire","əldə etmək","приобретать","verb","Students acquire new skills at school.","to learn something such as a language or a skill","əkˈwaɪər"],["assistance","kömək","помощь","noun","If you need assistance, ask your teacher.","help","əˈsɪstəns"],["attitude","münasibət, yanaşma","отношение","noun","A positive attitude helps you learn.","the way you feel about something or someone","ˈætəˌtud"],["hang out","vaxt keçirmək","проводить время","phrasal verb","I always hang out with my friends in the park after school.","to spend a lot of time with a person or in a place","hæŋ aʊt"],["hard skills","peşə (texniki) bacarıqları","профессиональные (технические) навыки","noun","Students spend a lot of time learning hard skills that are useful for their jobs.","specific, teachable abilities or skills that are acquired through training or experience and are typically related to technical knowledge","hɑrd skɪlz"],["influence","təsir etmək","влиять","noun","Friends can influence your decisions.","the power to have an effect on people or things, or a person or thing that is able to do this","ˈɪnfluəns"],["interact","ünsiyyət qurmaq","взаимодействовать","verb","Playing together helps us learn and interact with others.","to communicate with someone or react to something","ˌɪnərˈækt"],["non-technical","qeyri-texniki","нетехнический","adjective","Soft skills are non-technical skills.","not related to or involving specialised knowledge, skills, or procedures typically associated with a particular field or profession","nɑnˈtɛknɪkəl"]]},{"id":"6.2","title":"Vocabulary 2","words":[["outcome","nəticə","результат","noun","What was the outcome of the project?","the result of a particular action, event, or situation; the final or end result of a process or activity","ˈaʊtˌkəm"],["perform","yerinə yetirmək, çıxış etmək","выполнять, выступать","verb","She claims that she has a headache, so she cannot perform.","to do an action or piece of work","pərˈfɔrm"],["priceless","əvəzsiz, qiymətsiz","бесценный","adjective","The value of improving your soft skills is priceless.","used to describe a skill or quality that has a high value because it is very useful","ˈpraɪsləs"],["shared","ortaq","общий","adjective","Everyone's unique skills help the team achieve a shared goal.","owned, divided, felt, or experienced by more than one person","ʃɛrd"],["soft skills","yumşaq bacarıqlar","гибкие навыки","noun","Teachers gave advice to teenagers on soft skills.","personal characteristics or qualities that enable effective communication, interaction, and emotional intelligence, such as empathy and teamwork","sɔft skɪlz"],["step back","kənara çəkilmək","отойти в сторону","phrasal verb","I think I should step back now so that you can learn from this experience and grow.","to stop being involved in an activity or situation in order to think about it in a new way","stɛp bæk"],["support","dəstəkləmək","поддерживать","verb","Good friends support each other.","emotional or practical help","səˈpɔrt"]]},{"id":"6.3","title":"Reading","words":[["awkward","yöndəmsiz, narahat","неловкий","adjective","It was an awkward situation.","causing problems, worry or embarrassment","ˈɔkwərd"],["disappointed","məyus","разочарованный","adjective","I was disappointed with my test result.","feeling unhappy because something did not meet one's expectations or hopes","ˌdɪsəˈpɔɪnɪd"],["experienced","təcrübəli","опытный","adjective","Before I went to space, I was trained by experienced astronauts.","having skill or knowledge because you have done something many times","ɪkˈspɪriənst"],["fail","uğursuz olmaq","потерпеть неудачу","verb","Don't be afraid to fail.","not to succeed in what you are trying to achieve or are expected to do","feɪl"],["failure","uğursuzluq","неудача","noun","Don't be afraid of failure.","the fact of someone or something not succeeding","ˈfeɪljər"],["path","yol","путь","noun","It's a path to success.","a set of actions, especially ones that lead to a goal or result","pæθ"],["remind","xatırlatmaq","напоминать","verb","Please remind me about the test.","to cause someone to remember or recall something","riˈmaɪnd"],["resolve","həll etmək","разрешать, решать","verb","Good communication helps us resolve problems.","to solve or end a problem or difficulty","riˈzɑlv"],["responsible","məsul, cavabdeh","ответственный","adjective","Which part of the brain is responsible for laughing?","to have control and authority over something or someone and the duty of taking care of it, him or her","riˈspɑnsəbəl"],["unmotivated","motivasiyasız, həvəssiz","немотивированный","adjective","At those times, I felt sad and unmotivated.","not wanting to do something or not wanting to do something well","ʌnˈmoʊtɪveɪtɪd"],["weakness","zəiflik","слабость","noun","Asking for help is definitely not a sign of weakness.","a particular part or quality of someone or something that is not good or effective","ˈwiknəs"]]},{"id":"6.4","title":"Grammar A","words":[["culinary","kulinariya","кулинарный","adjective","He can go to VET school and study culinary there.","relating to cooking or the preparation of food, especially as an art or skill","ˈkjulɪˌnɛri"],["enrol","qeydiyyatdan keçmək, yazılmaq","записываться, поступать","verb","A lot more people have started to enrol in trade and technical schools.","to put yourself or someone else onto the official list of members of a course, college or group","ɪnˈroʊl"],["flexible","çevik","гибкий","adjective","Trade schools offer short and much more flexible programs.","able to change or be changed easily according to the situation","ˈflɛksəbəl"],["guarantee","zəmanət vermək","гарантировать","verb","Graduating from vocational schools might guarantee an early career start.","If something is guaranteed to happen or have a particular result, it is certain that it will happen or have that result","ˌgɛrənˈti"],["instructor","təlimatçı, müəllim","инструктор","noun","As always, our chef instructor was very helpful.","a person whose job is to teach people a practical skill","ˌɪnˈstrʌktər"],["vocational","peşə","профессиональный (о обучении)","adjective","In the past, fewer people showed interest in vocational schools.","relating to or providing practical skills and training that prepare individuals for specific jobs","voʊˈkeɪʃənəl"]]},{"id":"6.5","title":"Grammar B 1","words":[["amazed","heyrətlənmiş","изумлённый","adjective","The students were amazed when the magician made a rabbit disappear.","extremely surprised","əˈmeɪzd"],["awful","dəhşətli, çox pis","ужасный","adjective","My first performance was quite awful.","extremely bad","ˈɔfəl"],["be involved in something","nədəsə iştirak etmək","участвовать в чём-то","phrase","Azerbaijan is going to be involved in the exploration of outer space.","to participate in or take part in a particular activity, event or situation","bi ˌɪnˈvɑlvd ɪn ˈsʌmθɪŋ"],["boiling","çox isti, qaynar","очень жаркий, кипящий","adjective","It was boiling in the kitchen.","extremely hot","ˈbɔɪlɪŋ"],["delighted","çox məmnun","очень довольный","adjective","When I returned home, I was quite delighted.","very pleased","dɪˈlaɪtɪd"],["exhausted","çox yorğun, əldən düşmüş","измученный","adjective","I felt absolutely exhausted after my first day at trade school.","extremely tired","ɪgˈzɔstɪd"],["fantastic","əla, fantastik","фантастический","adjective","Her performance as a team leader was absolutely fantastic.","extremely good","fænˈtæstɪk"],["fascinating","çox maraqlı, valehedici","увлекательный","adjective","I found myself in some completely fascinating conversations about web designing challenges.","extremely interesting","ˈfæsəˌneɪtɪŋ"],["filthy","çox çirkli","грязный","adjective","Sometimes the kitchen can get filthy.","extremely dirty","ˈfɪlθi"]]},{"id":"6.6","title":"Grammar B 2","words":[["freezing","çox soyuq","ледяной","adjective","The only thing I don't like about studying in Canada is the freezing weather.","extremely cold","ˈfrizɪŋ"],["furious","qəzəbli","разъярённый","adjective","He was furious when he lost his phone.","extremely angry","fˈjʊriəs"],["get acquainted","tanış olmaq","познакомиться","phrase","On the first day, students get acquainted with their instructors.","to become familiar with or get to know someone or something","gɪt əkˈweɪnɪd"],["huge","nəhəng, çox böyük","огромный","adjective","Everyone who acts like that is a huge bookworm.","extremely large in size, amount or importance","juʤ"],["networking","əlaqə qurma","нетворкинг","noun","Networking events help you connect with people.","the process of meeting and talking to a lot of people, esp. in order to get information that can help you","ˈnɛtˌwərkɪŋ"],["push the boundaries","sərhədləri aşmaq","раздвигать границы","idiom","Try new things and push the boundaries.","to try to do your best and go beyond what you thought you could","pʊʃ ðʌ ˈbaʊndəriz"],["starving","çox ac","очень голодный","adjective","I was quite starving when the food was served.","extremely hungry","ˈstɑrvɪŋ"],["terrifying","qorxunc, dəhşətli","ужасающий","adjective","For me, it was really terrifying.","extremely frightening","ˈtɛrəˌfaɪɪŋ"],["tiny","çox kiçik","крошечный","adjective","There are tiny cues in body language.","extremely small in size or amount","ˈtaɪni"]]},{"id":"6.7","title":"Listening + Writing","words":[["alternative","alternativ","альтернативный","adjective","We need an alternative plan.","an alternative plan or method is one that you can use if you do not want to use another one","ɔlˈtɜrnətɪv"],["angle","yanaşma, bucaq","угол зрения","noun","Look at the problem from every angle.","a way of considering, dealing with something","ˈæŋgəl"],["beneficial","faydalı","полезный","adjective","It might not be beneficial to only stick to one way of thinking.","helpful, useful or good","ˌbɛnəˈfɪʃəl"],["collaboration","əməkdaşlıq","сотрудничество","noun","This method is a great tool for group collaboration and decision-making.","the act of working with another person or a group of people to create or produce something","kəˌlæbərˈeɪʃən"],["perspective","baxış bucağı","точка зрения","noun","Try to see the problem from a different perspective.","a way of thinking","pərˈspɛktɪv"],["summarise","xülasə etmək","обобщать","verb","Can you summarise the text?","to express the most important facts or ideas about something or someone in a short and clear form","ˈsʌməraɪz"],["stick to something","nəyəsə sadiq qalmaq","придерживаться чего-то","phrasal verb","To stay healthy, we should stick to a regular sleep schedule.","to continue doing or using something and not to want to change it","stɪk tɪ ˈsʌmθɪŋ"],["achievement","nailiyyət","достижение","noun","Write your biggest achievement in your CV.","something very good and difficult that you have succeeded in doing","əˈʧivmənt"],["confirm","təsdiq etmək","подтверждать","verb","Please confirm your email address.","to state or show that something is definitely true or correct, especially by providing evidence","kənˈfɜrm"]]},{"id":"6.8","title":"Time to Watch","words":[["approach","yanaşma","подход","noun","Every polyglot has a different approach to learning languages.","a way of considering or doing something","əˈproʊʧ"],["assertive","özünəinamlı, qətiyyətli","уверенный в себе, настойчивый","adjective","An assertive person says what he or she thinks without being rude.","Someone who is assertive behaves confidently and is not frightened to say what they want or believe","əˈsɜrtɪv"],["awareness","məlumatlılıq, şüurluluq","осознание","noun","Emotional intelligence starts with self-awareness.","knowing something; knowing that something exists and is important","əˈwɛrnəs"],["cue","işarə, siqnal","сигнал, подсказка","noun","A smile is a cue in body language.","a signal for someone to do something important","kju"],["deal with","öhdəsindən gəlmək, məşğul olmaq","справляться с","phrasal verb","EQ helps us deal with difficult situations.","to take action in order to achieve something or in order to solve a problem","dil wɪθ"],["depend","asılı olmaq","зависеть","verb","Success can depend on your soft skills.","to be influenced","dɪˈpɛnd"],["flaw","qüsur, nöqsan","недостаток","noun","Everyone has a flaw.","a mistake or weakness","flɔ"],["heartfelt","səmimi, ürəkdən gələn","искренний","adjective","She said a heartfelt thank you to her teacher.","strongly felt","ˈhɑrtˌfɛlt"],["insult","təhqir etmək","оскорблять","verb","Never insult other people.","to say or do something to someone that is rude","ˌɪnˈsʌlt"],["manage","idarə etmək","управлять","verb","Emotional intelligence is the ability to understand, use, and manage our emotions.","to control","ˈmænɪʤ"],["predict","proqnozlaşdırmaq","предсказывать","verb","A high EQ can predict success in social and emotional situations.","to say what you think will happen in the future","prɪˈdɪkt"],["priority","prioritet, üstünlük","приоритет","noun","Your health should be your priority.","something that is considered more important than other matters","praɪˈɔrəti"],["strive","səy göstərmək, çalışmaq","стремиться","verb","We should always strive to learn new things.","to try very hard to do something or to make something happen, especially for a long time or against difficulties","straɪv"]]}]}},"syn":{"1":[["provide","give"],["figure out","understand"],["appreciate","value"],["mysterious","strange"],["opportunity","chance"],["fault","mistake"],["request","ask"],["essential","necessary"],["imitate","copy"],["modern","new"],["film","movie"],["delicious","tasty"],["prove","show"],["transform","change"],["journalist","reporter"]],"2":[["photo","picture"],["discover","find"],["creature","animal"],["fact","truth"],["goal","aim"],["strange","unusual"],["home","house"],["finish","end"],["famous","popular"],["beautiful","nice"],["aeroplane","plane"],["create","make"],["protect","defend"],["emphasise","stress"],["achieve","reach"]],"3":[["realise","understand"],["amazing","wonderful"],["assist","help"],["receive","get"],["powerful","strong"],["disease","illness"],["mom","mother"],["talk","speak"],["look","see"],["big","large"],["journey","trip"],["tired","sleepy"],["exchange","swap"],["tricky","difficult"]],"4":[["flavour","taste"],["shop","store"],["incredible","amazing"],["happen","take place"],["rubbish","waste"],["trust","believe"],["dad","father"],["job","work"],["difficult","hard"],["cross","angry"],["amazing","awesome"],["strong","powerful"],["obtain","get"],["frightened","scared"]],"5":[["untidy","messy"],["grown-up","adult"],["peaceful","calm"],["damage","harm"],["struggle","fight"],["small","little"],["grandma","grandmother"],["yard","garden"],["street","road"],["clever","smart"],["kind","nice"],["give up","quit"],["hurt","harm"],["injury","wound"]],"6":[["tiny","small"],["huge","enormous"],["beneficial","useful"],["help","support"],["acquire","obtain"],["great","awesome"],["grandad","grandfather"],["right","correct"],["present","gift"],["start","begin"],["fast","quick"],["joy","happiness"],["entire","whole"],["elderly","old"]]},"ant":{"1":[["private","public"],["float","sink"],["clever","stupid"],["wonderful","terrible"],["relaxing","stressful"],["tall","short"],["start","finish"],["throw","catch"],["buy","sell"],["yes","no"],["brave","afraid"],["lose","find"],["true","false"],["rich","poor"],["positive","negative"]],"2":[["increase","decrease"],["fact","fiction"],["sweet","bitter"],["untidy","tidy"],["happy","sad"],["white","black"],["get up","go to bed"],["open","close"],["fun","boring"],["remember","forget"],["boring","interesting"],["win","lose"],["mental","physical"],["happiness","sadness"]],"3":[["damage","repair"],["safe","dangerous"],["high","low"],["crowded","empty"],["big","small"],["early","late"],["brother","sister"],["inside","outside"],["different","same"],["long","short"],["funny","serious"],["clean","dirty"],["danger","safety"],["kind","unkind"]],"4":[["polite","rude"],["agree","disagree"],["thick","thin"],["strange","normal"],["hot","cold"],["always","never"],["aunt","uncle"],["up","down"],["love","hate"],["on the left","on the right"],["strong","weak"],["excited","bored"],["known","unknown"],["elderly","young"]],"5":[["messy","tidy"],["peaceful","noisy"],["adult","child"],["question","answer"],["first","last"],["morning","evening"],["mom","dad"],["come","go"],["good","bad"],["behind","in front of"],["laugh","cry"],["ask","answer"],["ashamed","proud"],["birth","death"]],"6":[["huge","tiny"],["strength","weakness"],["success","failure"],["succeed","fail"],["old","young"],["day","night"],["grandma","grandad"],["teach","learn"],["before","after"],["slowly","quickly"],["less","more"],["real","fake"],["healthy","ill"],["ancient","modern"]]},"reading":{"1":{"title":"Why Is the Mother Tongue Important?","text":"Your mother tongue is a big part of your identity. Children who are good at their mother tongue are likely to learn and think faster. Knowing your native language helps you keep your cultural heritage alive and feel connected to your community. When you are fluent in your mother tongue, you can talk easily with older family members. Studying in your mother tongue can also help you get better results at school. And there is good news: fluency in your mother tongue makes learning other languages easier!","q":[["What is the mother tongue, according to the text?",["a big part of your identity","a difficult school subject","a foreign language"],0],["What can children who are good at their mother tongue do?",["learn and think faster","forget other languages","stop studying"],0],["Who can you talk to easily if you are fluent in your mother tongue?",["older family members","only teachers","tourists"],0],["What makes learning other languages easier?",["fluency in your mother tongue","watching TV","playing games"],0]]},"2":{"title":"The Benefits of Reading","text":"Reading is like a workout for your brain. When you dive into a good book, you improve your attention span and learn to concentrate. Reading also improves your literacy and your language skills. It increases your general knowledge, so you learn about the world without leaving your room. Fiction books take us on amazing adventures. They help us put ourselves in other people's shoes and understand their lives. So next time you have some free time, put your phone away and pick up a book!","q":[["What is reading like, according to the text?",["a workout for your brain","a waste of time","a difficult test"],0],["What does reading improve?",["your attention span","your sleep","your money"],0],["What do fiction books do?",["They take us on amazing adventures.","They give us money.","They make us tired."],0],["What should you do in your free time?",["pick up a book","play on your phone","sleep"],0]]},"3":{"title":"Why Do We Yawn?","text":"Have you ever wondered why we yawn, forget things or laugh? Scientists still have many questions. Some of them think that we yawn to cool down our brain. Others believe that yawning helps us stay alert. When you see someone yawn, you often yawn too! Our body clock also plays a big role. It tells us when to sleep and when to wake up. If we don't listen to our body clock, we can feel tired and our memory can become hazy.","q":[["Why do some scientists think we yawn?",["to cool down our brain","to make friends","to get food"],0],["What happens when you see someone yawn?",["You often yawn too.","You start laughing.","You go to bed."],0],["What does our body clock tell us?",["when to sleep and when to wake up","what to eat","where to go"],0],["What can happen if we don't listen to our body clock?",["Our memory can become hazy.","We can run faster.","We can learn more."],0]]},"4":{"title":"Life on Mars","text":"Would you like to live on Mars? Scientists are doing research to find out if people can survive there. Life on Mars would be challenging. There is no water available, and it is very cold. Astronauts would have to cope with isolation because they would be far away from their families. They would have to grow their own food in special settlements. Some people think this is insane, but others believe that one day humans will explore Mars and push the limits of what is possible.","q":[["What are scientists trying to find out?",["if people can survive on Mars","how to build cars","where the Moon is"],0],["Why would life on Mars be challenging?",["There is no water available.","There are too many people.","It is too hot."],0],["What would astronauts have to cope with?",["isolation","noisy neighbours","bad weather"],0],["Where would people grow food on Mars?",["in special settlements","in the jungle","in the mountains"],0]]},"5":{"title":"A Young Artist","text":"Aelita Andre is a young artist. She has visited London, Russia, Japan and New York. She started painting when she was only 9 months old! Her parents encouraged her to express their feelings through art. She paints on a big canvas, and when she paints, she thinks about the universe, animals and everything around her. People around the world admire her paintings, and some of them are very valuable. Her story inspires many children. It shows that imagination has no age. Some people may be sick with envy, but Aelita just loves to paint.","q":[["How old was Aelita when she started painting?",["9 months old","ten years old","two years old"],0],["What does she paint on?",["a big canvas","a wall","paper"],0],["What does she think about when she paints?",["the universe and animals","her homework","money"],0],["What does her story show?",["Imagination has no age.","Art is boring.","Painting is easy."],0]]},"6":{"title":"Soft Skills for Teenagers","text":"Today, knowledge is not enough to be successful. You also need soft skills. Teachers say that a positive attitude is very important. When you fail, don't be disappointed. Learn from your mistakes and try again. Critical thinking helps you look at a problem from every angle and make good decisions. Emotional intelligence helps you understand your feelings and the feelings of other people. Good communication helps you connect with people. If you support your friends and ask for assistance when you need it, the outcome will be better for everyone.","q":[["What else do you need to be successful?",["soft skills","a lot of money","good luck"],0],["What should you do when you fail?",["learn from your mistakes","give up","stop studying"],0],["What does critical thinking help you do?",["look at a problem from every angle","sleep better","forget problems"],0],["What does emotional intelligence help you understand?",["your feelings and the feelings of other people","math problems","foreign languages"],0]]}}};
